From: Local bring-up for FPT AX3000CV2 (WF-810DF)
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: yt921x: add tag_8021q plumbing

Teach the YT921x switch to speak plain 802.1Q on its CPU port so that
tag_yt921x_8021q can use the source-port VLANs of the tag_8021q
framework. The CPU port stops prepending its 8-byte tag, becomes a
VLAN-aware tagged member of every tag_8021q VLAN and forwards by the
VLAN table; a user port becomes an untagged member of its standalone or
bridge VLAN with that VLAN as PVID.

Because the tag_8021q core registers its VLANs before .port_setup runs,
the PVID it installs is shadowed in tag_8021q_pvid[] and re-applied
after yt921x_userport_standalone() resets the port. FDB and MDB entries
that the bridge hands over with VID 0 (the switch has no FDB isolation)
are translated to the standalone or bridge tag_8021q VID.

VLAN filtering, bridge VLANs and the 802.1Q uppers' TX path are
deliberately rejected in this mode; they need a second design pass.

---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.h
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.h
@@ -1376,6 +1376,12 @@
 	u32 policer_burst[YT921X_PORT_NUM];
 	u8 vlan_fid_mode;
 	u16 vlan_svl_fid;
+	/* the CPU port speaks plain 802.1Q (tag_yt921x_8021q), not its tag */
+	bool tag_8021q;
+	/* PVID the tag_8021q framework installed on the port, kept here
+	 * because port_setup() runs again after it and would reset it.
+	 */
+	u16 tag_8021q_pvid[YT921X_PORT_NUM];
 	bool devlink_params_registered;
 	int dt_rma_slow_action;
 	int dt_ctrlpkt_lldp_act;
